---
// SERVICES HUB — `/services/`. Rebuilt 2026-08-26 to docs/30-WEBSITE-MASTER-SPEC.md §18 (the
// route's job and visual direction) and §20A.20 (problem-chooser first, active directory second),
// with copy reconciled from docs/ASEPTACLEAN-SERVICE-LANDING-PAGE-SYSTEM.md §43–44 under the
// §20A.1 order: landing copy → map to current route → check active/gated state → check claims,
// pricing and scope → check current copy authority → then implement.
//
//   01 SERVICES HERO            ServicesHero            full-bleed photograph, left-aligned
//   02 PROBLEM CHOOSER          ServiceProblemChooser   six doors + the "not sure?" routing beat
//   03 CONDITION LEVELS         ServiceConditionLevels  routine vs detailed vs complex + reach
//   04 SERVICE DIRECTORY        ServiceDirectory        three real families, three visual weights
//   05 SCOPE / BOUNDARY         ServiceScopeBoundary    fit, exclusions, geography, disclaimer
//   06 HOW TO START + CTA       ServicesClose           four steps into one action
//
// WHAT THIS REPLACES. The previous page was PageHeader + a three-up pillar card grid restating
// homepage.serviceCards + ConfidenceAndFit + an embedded RequestForm: 568 words, zero images,
// three H2s, and a full lead form with a live Turnstile widget on a page whose job is routing.
//
// ROUTE STATE IS UNCHANGED AND DELIBERATELY SO. Same slug, same canonical, same sitemap
// membership, still indexable, same BreadcrumbList. No route was created, renamed, redirected or
// re-indexed by this pass, and no service's `publishStatus` moved. `/services/` remains the
// canonical services hub; AGENTS.md §2's narrowing (the prohibition targets `/services/{slug}`,
// not this hub) is what makes it legitimate, and nothing here adds a child route under it.
//
// SCHEMA IS BreadcrumbList ONLY, unchanged from the previous build and deliberately not extended.
// docs/21-CLAIMS-AND-COMPLIANCE-LAW.md §6.1's recommended set for a supporting page is exactly
// that, and doc 30 §20A.22 plus the task brief both say not to emit service schema for work
// outside current authority. `/` already emits Service nodes for the three families and one of
// them is under open owner review (see src/pages/index.astro) — adding a second, differently
// scoped set here would make two pages disagree about what Aseptaclean sells while that review
// is open.
//
// THE THREE RECONCILIATIONS THIS PAGE MAKES, all recorded in docs/05-DECISIONS-LOG.md 2026-08-26:
//   1. No rodent-droppings or pigeon-droppings routing, despite both appearing in the
//      landing-page system's chooser and directory. Cal. B&P §8550(a) + doc 21 §3, rank 3.
//   2. "South Bay & Peninsula", never "Santa Clara County". Owner ruling 2026-08-09.
//   3. No move-in route implied. Doc 30 §20A.3; move-in appears only inside the real route's
//      real label, "Move-in & move-out cleaning".
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ServiceConditionLevels from "@components/ServiceConditionLevels.astro";
import ServiceDirectory from "@components/ServiceDirectory.astro";
import ServiceProblemChooser from "@components/ServiceProblemChooser.astro";
import ServiceScopeBoundary from "@components/ServiceScopeBoundary.astro";
import ServicesClose from "@components/ServicesClose.astro";
import ServicesHero from "@components/ServicesHero.astro";
import { servicesHub } from "@data/servicePages";
import { site } from "@data/site";

const schema = [
  {
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: site.urls.home },
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: 2,
        name: "Services",
        item: new URL(servicesHub.slug, site.urls.site).href
      }
    ]
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={servicesHub.seoTitle}
  description={servicesHub.metaDescription}
  canonicalPath={servicesHub.slug}
  noindex={false}
  schema={schema}
>
  <ServicesHero />
  <ServiceProblemChooser />
  <ServiceConditionLevels />
  <ServiceDirectory />
  <ServiceScopeBoundary />
  <ServicesClose />
</BaseLayout>
